Some comments, i.e. yeses, below:

On Thu, Feb 19, 2015 at 7:15 PM, Bob Carpenter <ca...@alias-i.com> wrote:
> Would you like to move ShinyStan to the stan-dev repo?

Sure, that would be great. Because of the name change (SHINYstan to shinyStan) the new version I've been working on isn't in the jgabry/SHINYstan repository but rather at shinyStan/shinyStan <https://github.com/shinyStan/shinyStan>. The new one is the one we should move to stan-dev. The new version is basically ready to go (I'm just working on some tests) and I was thinking that the presentation at the nyhackR meetup <http://www.meetup.com/nyhackr/events/220598094/> on Wednesday would be a good time to make the new version public (well it's public already I suppose, but not annouced).

>
> Also, would you like us to add you as one of the Stan
> core developers?  It looks like Andrew wants to lean
> pretty heavily on ShinyStan going forward!

I would be honored. You guys have really done an amazing job and Stan is such an important contribution to statistics and every other field that relies on statistics. Working on shinyStan is by far the most enjoyable work I've been doing and I'd love to work with you in whatever capacity helps Stan moving forward.

Jonah

