I wanted to do the leukemia GP survival model in BDA3 with Stan, and first started experimenting with the following simpler GP classification model, which also shows how I would like to define GPs by combining basic covariance functions. With 250 data points Stan gives high N_eff, but sampling is very slow (N_eff/s<1.7e-02 and 5.5 hours to get total of 200 saved iterations from 4 chains (for comparison MML estimate with GPstuff takes less than 1.5s)). With 1000 data points I run out of memory in my laptop (using top, I can see the process going over 5GB before dying (for comparison MML estimate with GPstuff takes 45s, and less than 1GB memory)). Comaprison to MML with GPstuff is not fair, but I was still surprised that Stan for GP is so slow and that running out of memory with 1000 data points. We have had discussion on things which could make GPs faster in Stan. Feel free to use this example for testing (sorry for not including R code, and I guess the Matlab code would not be so useful for you).

